0..77 Comment "// This source writes a map\'s action on a path as a transport, after the HoTT"
78..100 Comment "// book\'s Lemma 2.2.1."
101..103 Comment "//"
104..182 Comment "// The defined path operations write `Path.ap` so. The definition must convert"
183..234 Comment "// with the native form at a presented type\'s cell."
235..237 Comment "//"
238..312 Comment "// The transport starts at reflexivity on the map\'s image of the start. It"
313..388 Comment "// carries that path along the path, in the family of paths from the image."
389..468 Comment "// The family calls the map through the definition\'s parameter. At the loop the"
469..546 Comment "// transport reads the map that the call binds. It computes by the map\'s loop"
547..584 Comment "// arm, as the native `Path.ap` does."
585..587 Comment "//"
588..603 Comment "// - see: #5206"
604..651 Comment "// - see: #5481 — `alongFlipped`, `alongKept`"
653..693 Comment "// The circle and its flip, `invLooper`."
